{"name":"Super Saiyan","hex":"#ffdd00","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"super","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of excellent quality, superfine.","Better than average, better than usual; wonderful."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Very; extremely (used like the prefix super-).","Absolutely; utterly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/super"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dragon Ball","blocks":[{"text":"Dragon Ball  is a Japanese media franchise created by Akira Toriyama. The series follows the adventures of protagonist Son Goku from his childhood through adulthood as he trains in martial arts. Along his journey, he makes several friends, becomes a family man, discovers his alien heritage, and battles a wide variety of villains, many of whom, like him, seek the mystical orbs called the Dragon Balls in order to summon a wish-granting dragon."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Ball","wikidata":"Q2020"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/05/Wiki_DragonBall_Earth.png/500px-Wiki_DragonBall_Earth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/05/Wiki_DragonBall_Earth.png/500px-Wiki_DragonBall_Earth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Earth of Dragon Ball, as published in Daizenshuu 4: World Guide","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWiki_DragonBall_Earth.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/24/Weekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_%28Dec._1984%29_is_the_first_appearance_of_Goku._Cover_art_by_Akira_Toriyama.jpg/250px-Weekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_%28Dec._1984%29_is_the_first_appearance_of_Goku._Cover_art_by_Akira_Toriyama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/24/Weekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_%28Dec._1984%29_is_the_first_appe